  "rationale": "The archived probe shows both public instances fail with plan_length 0 and plan_semantics, and whitespace normalization did not help, so the fault is semantic. Reviewing the source: (1) ground argument order is wrong in a way no normalization fixes; (2) there is no drop action, yet tighten_nut's STRIPS effect removes useable and the man keeps carrying, making goals unreachable after one nut; (3) tightened facts in init are ignored, so pre-tightened nuts count as needing work. The candidate fixes all three: exact PDDL parameter order, adds drop, reads initial tightened, uses BFS over the full lifted model with directed links. Uncertainty: this is static reasoning only; I have not executed it, and the evaluator may impose syntax checks I cannot see. BFS over the full state space may blow up on larger hidden instances (no heuristic or pruning), which is a real risk I cannot verify. n_params stays 3 since the domain model is unchanged.",
